--- Completion 3 ---
To find the position of the dark grey l-shaped countertop with respect to the brown colour cube-shaped wooden material, I need to use the Object Detector Tool. I will need to provide the image file path and the labels 'baseball' and 'basket' to identify the countertop and the wooden material, respectively. I will save the detected objects as images if the save_object parameter is set to True and the saved_image_path is provided.

```python
import Object_Detector_Tool

# Parameters for Object Detector Tool
image_path = 'path/to/codesk.jpg'  # Replace this with the actual image path
labels = ['baseball', 'basket']
save_object = True  # Setting to True to save detected objects
saved_image_path = 'detected_objects'

# Execute Object Detector Tool
detected_objects, object_number = Object_Detector_Tool.execute(image=image_path, labels=labels, save_object=save_object, saved_image_path=saved_image_path)

# Extract the position of the dark grey l-shaped countertop
dark_gray_position = {"x0": detected_objects["baseball"][0]["bbox"][0], "y0": detected_objects["baseball"][0]["bbox"][1], "x1": detected_objects["baseball"][1]["bbox"][0], "y1": detected_objects["baseball"][1]["bbox"][1], "x2": detected_objects["baseball"][2]["bbox"][0], "y2": detected_objects["baseball"][2]["bbox"][1]}

# Extract the position of the brown cube-shaped wooden material
brown_cube_position = {"x0": detected_objects["basket"][0]["bbox"][0], "y0": detected_objects["basket"][0]["bbox"][1], "x1": detected_objects["basket"][1]["bbox"][0], "y1": detected_objects["basket"][1]["bbox"][1], "x2": detected_objects["basket"][2]["bbox"][0], "y2": detected_objects["basket"][2]["bbox"][1]}

# Calculate the distance between the countertop and the wooden material
distance = (dark_gray_position["x2"] - brown_cube_position["x0"]) ** 2 + (dark_gray_position["y2"] - brown_cube_position["y0"]) ** 2 ** 0.5

# Print the distance
print(distance)
```

After running this Python program, you will get the distance of the dark grey l-shaped countertop from the brown cube-shaped wooden material, which can be used to answer your question.
